Z||000009||danny boy||05-16-2001||09:52 PM|||| Ahh, yes. My job sucks.I'm constantly broke. For the last, oh, 6 months I have been absolutely miserable. I hate everything. I have no friends unless someone needs something. ALL of my cars are junk.<BR>  One night a few years ago I was sitting at the bar with my dad taking the usual abuse from everyone there and someone asked what I was going to do with my life.I was going to school for CADD and I had just quit my night job at the hospital(got stuck with a needle some ahole doctor threw in the garbage,If it would have beed contaminated....)so of course I was the lazy no good again. I replied jokingly "maybe I'll drive truck" which got the response from dad "sh1t boy, you couldn't do it. Next thng I know I'm on my way to Nashville,TN to drive for Proline.<BR> Anyway 6 months ago I was told get a local job or find another girl to marry. I took a 20K/year paycut and came home.<BR> Now I'm depressed all the time to the point that my cars don't even make me happy.I hate working on them(my paintjob has been a 2month long project), I don't even enjoy driving the Stealth. <BR>In short, life sucks. Theres way more to say, but I'm sure no one wants to hear it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||KissMySSFiero||05-16-2001||11:28 PM||||last tues i spent my 21st birthday alone.  very depressing.  I just moved and i havent done a damn thing exciting yet.  other than car stuff.  which isnt cutting it.  all i think about is my girlfriend that i left in fla.  i called her one day about a week after i got here.  she was out withsome guy.  in the car and told me the radio was too loud as she was turning it up.  then she hung up.  i figured fine. ill get over it an move on.  well i was doin fine. then she talked to me a couple weeks later and said she was worried about me because i havent talked to her in a while.  she swore they were just friends.  funny.  ive never met him or heard of him.  but they were best friends.  anyways.  im 21 now.  im a good lookin guy but the only girls i get are seekin me cuz there Bf pissed them off and im the one night stand type thing.  not bad but i do want more.  or i get the 16 year old high school chic who has to ask daddy if she can stay out til 11.  either way i get the sharp end of the stick and it never gets better.  look at it this way.  you have friends there for  you now.  they may be gettin married but at least youve got someone there your age.  the only people i know here are my family.  and they are all old to me.  there is no chance of me finding a nice lady friend when im hangin out with mommy.  life sucks sometimes.  spank it go to sleep and look foward to tomorrow.  it can only get better.||||reg||1
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||05-17-2001||09:02 AM||||Well, don't know if it'll make you feel any better, but here's my tale of woe...<P>I'm 32, tall, slim, smart, skilled, decently put together, neat, good-looking (so I'm told - some days I see it, some days I don't), was married for the last 5 years, did the permanent split thing with her last November... I *would* be doing pretty decent financially if we'd kept the marriage thing going together, but since we didn't, I moved out (the house was hers - she had bought it about 6 months before we met) and got an apartment 5 minutes from work (I'd been driving 45 min.-an hour *each way* every day to work and back for the last 5 years), but now being a one-income household is killing me... <P>She so *very* much wants to work out a friendship out of all this, but I'm starting to think that the only reason she has for this is so *she* doesn't feel as guilty about (evidently) taking 90% of my friends away from me right along with her... we've all been members of the same stage-combat/swordfighting group for the last ten years (which means I knew them for twice as long as any of us had known her), but since she and I broke up, I seem to be completely 'out of sight, out of mind' with them... so, I hang with the remaining 10% of my friends (Hi, Formula88!) doing Fiero stuff, or movies, or whatever I can for free, since money is so tight...<P>I've tried the online personal ad thing, and the newspaper classified personal ad thing, and the only response I'd had there was a phone call from a perfect-sounding 25y.o. 100#, 5'-5" blonde, blue-eyed gal who saw my ad in the paper - but between the time she called me and the day we were supposed to go out to meet two days later, she met some other guy and they were "getting along really well" (as she put it when I called to reschedule our date after she left a message cancelling it that morning), so even *that* has been a total crapout.<P>Yeah... whoohoo... single life is just flippin' dandy, don'tcha know... yippee. :rolleyes||||reg||1
